                <pb facs="0333" n="329" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg329"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.512/1518: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-05-22T10:00:00+08:00">May 22, 1938—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 22—7 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>262. Your 154, May 21, 2 p.m.<anchor n="23" xml:id="d433-f1"/> Following is my
                    reply to Tientsin’s May 13, 5 p.m. in regard to certain land tax matters.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“May [16], 11 a.m. Your May 13, 5 p.m. I suggest that you use your own
                        judgment in this matter and be guided by my May 7, 10 a.m. should you decide
                        to advise compliance.”</p>
                </quote>
                <p>My May 7, 10 a.m. referred to above repeated to Tientsin the Department’s 141,
                    May 5, 7 [<hi rendition="#italic">4</hi>] p.m. and instructed Caldwell to be
                    guided accordingly.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
